WEBVTT

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.554
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.482
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:19.483 --> 00:00:20.805
The family business.

00:00:22.766 --> 00:00:25.904
You know the truth about
Sammy and the other children.

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:29.142
I've known for a while.

00:00:29.156 --> 00:00:30.760
Dad, you know the demon

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.611
He said he had plans for
me and children like me.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.047
Do you have any idea
what he meant by that?

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.613
No, I don't.

00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:38.290
Did he say anything to you?

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:40.779
No.

00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:43.511
Nothing.

00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:47.138
Max, your abilities started
6,7 months ago, right?

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:49.503
How'd you know that? 'Cause
that's when my abilities started.

00:00:49.535 --> 00:00:50.450
You and I...

00:00:50.538 --> 00:00:52.280
We're chosen. For what?

00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:53.422
I don't know.

00:00:53.435 --> 00:00:55.451
Everyone's capable of murder. Everyone.

00:00:55.465 --> 00:00:57.573
You know, maybe that's what
the demon's doing, pushing us,

00:00:57.607 --> 00:00:58.911
Finding ways to break us.

00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.083
Sam, we don't know what the demon wants.

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:02.522
We all have some kind
of ability. Ability?

00:01:02.605 --> 00:01:04.443
Psychic ability. I have visions,

00:01:04.535 --> 00:01:06.632
Premonitions. It's
different for everybody.

00:01:06.657 --> 00:01:09.293
The demon said he had
plans for people like us.

00:01:09.356 --> 00:01:11.700
What kind of plans? We
don't really know for sure.

00:01:14.627 --> 00:01:15.901
Don't be afraid, Scott.

00:01:15.996 --> 00:01:17.521
You can tell me anything. You know that.

00:01:18.716 --> 00:01:20.990
Whatever you say, it
won't leave this room.

00:01:24.488 --> 00:01:26.702
It started a little over a year ago.

00:01:28.155 --> 00:01:29.881
Migraines at first.

00:01:31.128 --> 00:01:34.272
Then I found I could do stuff.

00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:36.581
What do you mean, "do stuff"?

00:01:37.805 --> 00:01:39.452
I have this ability.

00:01:41.096 --> 00:01:42.522
When I touch something,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.781
I can electrocute it if I want.

00:01:48.038 --> 00:01:49.351
How do you know?

00:01:51.605 --> 00:01:53.563
Did it to the neighbor's cat.

00:01:55.688 --> 00:01:58.342
Its insides fried up like a hamburger.

00:02:03.098 --> 00:02:04.312
You don't believe me.

00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:09.422
I believe that you believe it.

00:02:11.708 --> 00:02:12.633
Then here.

00:02:13.307 --> 00:02:14.943
Want to shake on it?

00:02:26.595 --> 00:02:29.131
Why would you want to kill
the neighbor's cat, Scott?

00:02:29.217 --> 00:02:30.442
I don't.

00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:34.351
He wants me to and he
doesn't want me to stop there.

00:02:34.426 --> 00:02:35.471
Who?

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:38.761
The yellow-Eyed man.

00:02:39.226 --> 00:02:41.130
He comes to me in my dreams.

00:02:41.705 --> 00:02:44.280
He tells me to do things, awful things

00:02:44.878 --> 00:02:46.791
But I tell him no.

00:02:47.826 --> 00:02:49.440
"No, I don't want to!"

00:02:50.386 --> 00:02:52.802
What else does the
yellow-Eyed man tell you?

00:02:58.007 --> 00:02:59.733
He has plans for me.

00:02:59.756 --> 00:03:01.383
What kind of plans?

00:03:03.118 --> 00:03:07.262
And you've just had
some kind of mushroom

00:03:07.265 --> 00:03:11.841
And your mind is moving low

00:03:11.848 --> 00:03:15.560
Go ask Alice

00:03:15.925 --> 00:03:18.723
I think she'll know

00:03:21.377 --> 00:03:24.911
When logic and proportion

00:03:25.008 --> 00:03:25.902
Hello?

00:03:25.956 --> 00:03:29.851
Have fallen softly dead

00:03:29.867 --> 00:03:34.542
And the white knight
is talking backwards

00:03:34.606 --> 00:03:38.822
And the red queen's, "off with her head"

00:03:39.596 --> 00:03:41.990
Remember

00:03:42.516 --> 00:03:46.030
What the dormouse said

00:03:48.028 --> 00:03:49.942
Feed your head

00:04:07.705 --> 00:04:09.311
Before dad died, he...

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.402
He told me something.

00:04:13.356 --> 00:04:14.902
Something about you.

00:04:16.736 --> 00:04:17.983
What?

00:04:21.737 --> 00:04:23.401
Dean, what did he tell you?

00:04:24.466 --> 00:04:25.423
He said that he...

00:04:26.578 --> 00:04:28.510
Wanted me to watch out for you...

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.052
Take care of you.

00:04:32.006 --> 00:04:33.873
He told you that a million times.

00:04:33.926 --> 00:04:35.240
Well, this time was different.

00:04:36.745 --> 00:04:38.040
He said that I had to...

00:04:39.576 --> 00:04:40.790
Save you.

00:04:42.225 --> 00:04:43.571
Save me from what?

00:04:43.665 --> 00:04:45.543
He just said that I had to save you

00:04:45.545 --> 00:04:46.792
And nothing else mattered

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:49.712
And that if I couldn't, I'd...

00:04:50.648 --> 00:04:52.422
You'd what, Dean?

00:04:53.857 --> 00:04:55.273
I'd have to kill you.

00:05:00.037 --> 00:05:02.552
He said that I might
have to kill you, Sammy.

00:05:03.128 --> 00:05:04.282
Kill me?

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:09.070
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:05:09.135 --> 00:05:09.931
I don't know.

00:05:10.007 --> 00:05:12.153
He must have had some kinda
reason for saying it, right?

00:05:12.866 --> 00:05:14.291
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:05:14.338 --> 00:05:16.322
Am I supposed to go
dark side or something?

00:05:17.018 --> 00:05:19.503
What else did he say,
Dean? That's it, I swear.

00:05:19.536 --> 00:05:21.692
How could you not have told
me this? Because it was dad,

00:05:21.727 --> 00:05:23.461
And he begged me not to. Who cares!

00:05:23.496 --> 00:05:25.820
Take some responsibility
for yourself, Dean!

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:28.001
You had no right to keep this from me!

00:05:28.106 --> 00:05:29.362
You  think I wanted this?

00:05:29.838 --> 00:05:30.882
Huh?

00:05:31.007 --> 00:05:33.360
I wish to god he'd
never opened his mouth.

00:05:34.027 --> 00:05:37.171
Then I wouldn't have to walk around
with this screaming in my head all day!

00:05:44.516 --> 00:05:46.160
We each got to figure
out what's going on,

00:05:46.166 --> 00:05:47.852
Then, what the hell all this means.

00:05:50.515 --> 00:05:51.583
We do?

00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:54.680
I've been thinking about this.
I think we should just lay low,

00:05:54.727 --> 00:05:56.870
You  know. At least for a while.

00:05:56.916 --> 00:05:58.263
It would be safer.

00:05:59.347 --> 00:06:01.011
That way, I could make sure...

00:06:01.106 --> 00:06:02.102
What?

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:04.772
That I don't turn evil?

00:06:04.795 --> 00:06:07.420
That I don't turn into
some kind of killer?

00:06:07.426 --> 00:06:09.132
I never said that.
Jeez, you're not careful,

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:10.850
You will have to waste me one day, Dean.

00:06:10.957 --> 00:06:12.092
I never said that!

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:16.233
Damn it, Sam, this whole thing
is spinning out of control.

00:06:16.756 --> 00:06:19.421
All right? You're immune
to some weirdo demon virus

00:06:20.527 --> 00:06:22.542
And I don't even know
what the hell anymore.

00:06:26.236 --> 00:06:29.151
And you're pissed at me, and I
get it. That's fine. I deserve it.

00:06:31.035 --> 00:06:33.993
But we lay low until we
figure out our next move, okay?

00:06:34.076 --> 00:06:35.280
Forget it.

00:06:37.246 --> 00:06:39.232
Sam, please, man.

00:06:39.328 --> 00:06:41.023
Hey, please.

00:06:42.408 --> 00:06:44.171
Just give me some time.

00:06:44.948 --> 00:06:46.300
Give me some time to think, okay?

00:06:46.336 --> 00:06:49.032
I'm begging you here. Please, please...

00:09:15.637 --> 00:09:16.521
Honey?

00:09:18.597 --> 00:09:19.841
Are you okay?

00:09:20.107 --> 00:09:21.612
Oh, I just had another nightmare.

00:09:21.698 --> 00:09:23.120
It's fine. It's nothing.

00:09:23.227 --> 00:09:24.721
Just go back to sleep.

00:09:25.346 --> 00:09:26.522
Sure?

00:09:27.576 --> 00:09:29.382
Yeah. Okay.

00:09:49.558 --> 00:09:50.512
Sam.

00:09:50.735 --> 00:09:51.903
Hey, Ellen.

00:09:54.446 --> 00:09:56.563
You don't seem that surprised to see me.

00:09:56.597 --> 00:09:58.123
Your brother's been
calling, worry to say,

00:09:58.126 --> 00:09:59.613
Looking for you. Yeah.

00:10:00.045 --> 00:10:01.301
I figured he might.

00:10:01.337 --> 00:10:03.111
What's going on between you two?

00:10:05.525 --> 00:10:06.620
So, um...

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:08.999
How's Jo?

00:10:11.452 --> 00:10:13.061
Well, I don't really know.

00:10:13.107 --> 00:10:15.528
What do you mean? I
haven't seen her in weeks.

00:10:15.609 --> 00:10:17.441
She sends a postcard now and again.

00:10:17.467 --> 00:10:18.731
Well, what happened?

00:10:18.747 --> 00:10:21.462
Well, after she worked
that job with you boys

00:10:21.537 --> 00:10:23.343
She decided she wanted
to keep on hunting.

00:10:23.946 --> 00:10:25.690
I said, "not under my roof,"

00:10:25.696 --> 00:10:27.853
And she said "fine".

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:33.300
So I'm probably the last person
you want to see right now.

00:10:35.138 --> 00:10:37.672
Oh, don't get me wrong.

00:10:37.758 --> 00:10:40.733
I wish I could blame
the hell out of you boys.

00:10:41.466 --> 00:10:42.721
It would be easier.

00:10:42.788 --> 00:10:45.710
The truth is, it's not your fault.

00:10:46.137 --> 00:10:47.430
Sam,

00:10:48.016 --> 00:10:49.512
None of it is.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:53.980
I want you to know that

00:10:54.597 --> 00:10:57.023
I forgave your daddy a long time ago...

00:10:58.075 --> 00:10:59.890
For what happened to my Bill.

00:11:01.557 --> 00:11:04.041
I just don't think he
ever forgave himself.

00:11:05.068 --> 00:11:06.702
What did happen?

00:11:10.585 --> 00:11:13.653
Um, so, why did you come here, sweetie?

00:11:15.527 --> 00:11:16.853
I need help.

00:11:17.006 --> 00:11:18.672
So, what am I looking for, Sam?

00:11:18.715 --> 00:11:20.620
Other people, other...

00:11:21.066 --> 00:11:22.793
Psychics like me.

00:11:22.897 --> 00:11:26.201
As many as possible and I
need a nationwide search.

00:11:26.256 --> 00:11:27.382
But

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:29.691
I thought there was no
way to track them all down.

00:11:29.786 --> 00:11:32.121
Not all of them had
nursery fires like you did.

00:11:32.605 --> 00:11:33.522
Well...

00:11:33.525 --> 00:11:35.503
No, but some had to.

00:11:35.547 --> 00:11:36.591
Start there.

00:11:40.815 --> 00:11:41.653
Done...

00:11:41.656 --> 00:11:42.902
And done.

00:11:43.007 --> 00:11:44.681
That was fast. Well,

00:11:44.717 --> 00:11:46.601
Apparently, that's my job.

00:11:46.686 --> 00:11:48.911
Make the monkey dance. Key boarding.

00:11:48.935 --> 00:11:50.683
Just tell us what you got, Ash.

00:11:50.718 --> 00:11:54.430
Four folks fit the profile nationwide.

00:11:54.487 --> 00:11:57.360
Born in '83, mother
died in a nursery fire,

00:11:57.396 --> 00:11:59.412
The whole shebang. Four? That's it?

00:11:59.438 --> 00:12:02.422
Sam Winchester from Lawrence, Kansas.

00:12:02.486 --> 00:12:04.162
Max Miller from Saginaw, Michigan,

00:12:04.168 --> 00:12:06.650
Andrew Gallagher from Guthrie, Oklahoma

00:12:07.547 --> 00:12:08.610
And

00:12:08.625 --> 00:12:10.473
Another name,

00:12:10.478 --> 00:12:11.692
Scott Carey.

00:12:13.755 --> 00:12:15.041
What? You got an address?

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:16.181
Kind of.

00:12:16.778 --> 00:12:21.671
The arbor hills cemetery
in Lafayette, Indiana.

00:12:21.735 --> 00:12:24.201
Plot 486. So he's dead?

00:12:24.297 --> 00:12:27.103
Killed about a month ago. Killed how?

00:12:27.136 --> 00:12:28.370
Stabbed.

00:12:28.808 --> 00:12:30.103
Parking lot.

00:12:30.788 --> 00:12:32.502
Fuzz don't have much.

00:12:32.985 --> 00:12:34.453
No suspects.

00:12:37.588 --> 00:12:38.490
All right.

00:12:38.787 --> 00:12:40.153
Thank you.

00:12:45.017 --> 00:12:47.012
Where are you going? Indiana.

00:12:47.097 --> 00:12:48.071
Sam,

00:12:48.937 --> 00:12:51.043
I got to call Dean. I've got
to let him know where you are.

00:12:51.116 --> 00:12:53.442
Ellen, I'm trying to find answers

00:12:53.447 --> 00:12:55.062
About who I am

00:12:55.567 --> 00:12:58.893
And my brother means well, but
he can't protect me from that.

00:13:00.707 --> 00:13:01.911
Please.

00:13:07.417 --> 00:13:09.430
You said you went to
high school with Scott?

00:13:10.038 --> 00:13:11.932
Uh, yes, sir, I did.

00:13:12.248 --> 00:13:15.133
I just heard about what
happened. I'm so sorry.

00:13:15.548 --> 00:13:16.922
Scotty was a good boy.

00:13:18.018 --> 00:13:19.931
He changed a lot since you knew him.

00:13:19.977 --> 00:13:21.513
What do you mean?

00:13:21.917 --> 00:13:25.323
It started about a year
ago with these headaches.

00:13:25.428 --> 00:13:28.383
Then he got depressed, paranoid.

00:13:28.856 --> 00:13:30.920
Nightmares. Nightmares?

00:13:33.878 --> 00:13:36.903
Did he ever talk to you about
his nightmares, what he saw?

00:13:37.006 --> 00:13:38.030
No, no,

00:13:38.567 --> 00:13:40.003
He  closed up on me.

00:13:40.017 --> 00:13:42.373
I  tried to get him
help, but nothing took.

00:13:43.105 --> 00:13:44.233
He'd just...

00:13:45.036 --> 00:13:47.212
Lock himself in his room for days.

00:13:48.506 --> 00:13:50.540
You think maybe I could see his room?

00:15:10.337 --> 00:15:11.932
Who are you? Please...

00:15:12.555 --> 00:15:13.921
You're in danger.

00:15:15.055 --> 00:15:17.761
Okay, look, I know how all this sounds,

00:15:17.766 --> 00:15:20.500
But I am not insane,
and I'm not on drugs.

00:15:20.607 --> 00:15:22.163
Okay, I am normal,

00:15:22.195 --> 00:15:24.862
And this is way, way off the map for me.

00:15:24.887 --> 00:15:26.012
All right, all right, just...

00:15:26.596 --> 00:15:28.602
Just calm down, okay?

00:15:29.328 --> 00:15:31.210
What's your name? Ava.

00:15:31.257 --> 00:15:32.623
Ava? Ava Wilson.

00:15:32.668 --> 00:15:35.070
Ava, I'm Sam Winchester, all right?

00:15:35.146 --> 00:15:38.730
Now, you were telling me
about these dreams of yours?

00:15:38.798 --> 00:15:40.661
Oh, yeah, uh, okay.

00:15:40.667 --> 00:15:44.223
About a year ago, I started having
these like headaches, and just...

00:15:44.538 --> 00:15:47.361
Nightmares, I guess. And I
really didn't think much of it

00:15:47.465 --> 00:15:51.671
Until I had this one dream where I saw
this guy get stabbed in a parking lot.

00:15:53.006 --> 00:15:54.442
When was this?

00:15:54.486 --> 00:15:57.160
Uh, about a month ago. But anyway,

00:15:57.205 --> 00:15:58.980
A couple of days later...

00:16:00.547 --> 00:16:02.071
I found this.

00:16:05.655 --> 00:16:07.901
I saw this guy die

00:16:07.906 --> 00:16:10.270
Days before it happened.

00:16:10.296 --> 00:16:13.313
I don't know why. I don't
know. It's just for some reason,

00:16:14.007 --> 00:16:16.693
My dreams are coming true,

00:16:16.708 --> 00:16:17.901
And

00:16:17.908 --> 00:16:19.600
Last night,

00:16:19.608 --> 00:16:21.383
I had another one.

00:16:22.065 --> 00:16:23.172
Okay.

00:16:23.248 --> 00:16:24.681
About you.

00:16:26.688 --> 00:16:28.640
I saw you die.

00:16:32.737 --> 00:16:34.032
How did you find me?

00:16:35.307 --> 00:16:37.971
You had motel stationery,
and I googled the motel,

00:16:38.057 --> 00:16:41.173
And it was real, and so I
just thought that I should

00:16:41.177 --> 00:16:42.620
Warn you.

00:16:44.538 --> 00:16:45.822
I don't believe this.

00:16:47.297 --> 00:16:48.851
Of course you don't.

00:16:48.926 --> 00:16:50.972
You think I'm a total nutjob.

00:16:51.208 --> 00:16:52.802
Wait! No, no, no.

00:16:52.886 --> 00:16:54.972
I mean, you must be one of us.

00:16:55.707 --> 00:16:58.283
Sorry, one of... One of who?

00:16:58.468 --> 00:17:01.191
One of the psychics, like me.

00:17:01.705 --> 00:17:02.773
Look, Ava, I have visions too, all
right? So... so we're connected.

00:17:09.287 --> 00:17:11.872
Okay, so... you're nuts.

00:17:11.918 --> 00:17:14.510
That's great. No,
okay, okay. Okay, look.

00:17:14.545 --> 00:17:17.551
Did your mother happen
to die in a house fire?

00:17:17.645 --> 00:17:20.013
No, my mother lives in Palm Beach.

00:17:20.075 --> 00:17:22.021
So you don't fit the pattern either.

00:17:29.036 --> 00:17:30.032
Hello?

00:17:30.077 --> 00:17:31.021
It's Ellen.

00:17:31.055 --> 00:17:32.453
Hey, have you heard from Sam?

00:17:32.557 --> 00:17:33.481
I have.

00:17:33.486 --> 00:17:36.843
But he made me promise not
to tell you where he is.

00:17:36.867 --> 00:17:38.301
Come on, Ellen, please.

00:17:38.407 --> 00:17:40.343
Something bad could be
going on here, and I swore

00:17:40.348 --> 00:17:41.703
I'd look after that kid.

00:17:41.758 --> 00:17:44.830
Dean, let's say you can't
protect your loved ones forever.

00:17:46.458 --> 00:17:47.803
Well, I say screw that.

00:17:47.846 --> 00:17:49.290
What else is family for?

00:17:51.007 --> 00:17:52.853
He's in Lafayette, Indiana.

00:17:53.687 --> 00:17:54.642
Thanks.

00:17:56.075 --> 00:17:57.773
Why can't you just leave town,

00:17:57.778 --> 00:17:59.503
Please, before you blow up?

00:18:00.575 --> 00:18:01.752
No, I can't.

00:18:01.848 --> 00:18:04.522
Oh, god. Why not?

00:18:04.708 --> 00:18:06.952
Because there's something
going on here, Ava,

00:18:07.456 --> 00:18:08.861
With you, with me.

00:18:09.027 --> 00:18:11.082
I mean, there are
others like us out there

00:18:11.167 --> 00:18:13.523
And we're all a part of something,

00:18:14.098 --> 00:18:15.750
And I've got to figure out what.

00:18:15.836 --> 00:18:17.760
Okay, you know what?

00:18:18.277 --> 00:18:20.000
Screw you, buddy. Okay?

00:18:20.036 --> 00:18:22.830
'Cause I'm a secretary from Peoria
and I'm not part of anything.

00:18:23.486 --> 00:18:24.361
Do you see this?

00:18:24.395 --> 00:18:26.620
I am getting married in eight weeks.

00:18:26.706 --> 00:18:28.613
I am supposed to be at
home addressing invitations

00:18:28.655 --> 00:18:31.073
Which I am way behind on, by the way.

00:18:31.127 --> 00:18:34.611
But instead, I drove out
here to save your weirdo ass.

00:18:34.698 --> 00:18:38.352
But if you just want to
stay here and die, fine.

00:18:38.585 --> 00:18:39.652
Me?

00:18:39.706 --> 00:18:41.702
I'm due back on planet earth.

00:18:41.787 --> 00:18:43.642
Don't you wanna know
why this is happening?

00:18:45.355 --> 00:18:48.043
I mean, don't these visions
scare the hell out of you?

00:18:49.597 --> 00:18:51.923
'Cause if you walk out
that door right now,

00:18:53.237 --> 00:18:55.141
You might never know the truth.

00:18:59.025 --> 00:19:00.563
I need your help.

00:19:00.648 --> 00:19:02.733
So, Miss Wilson, you're new in town?

00:19:03.328 --> 00:19:04.461
That's right.

00:19:04.537 --> 00:19:06.982
And what made you decide
to seek out therapy?

00:19:08.507 --> 00:19:10.161
I have no idea.

00:19:10.557 --> 00:19:11.510
No?

00:19:11.596 --> 00:19:14.732
No, I mean, I'm feeling really, super...

00:19:15.568 --> 00:19:17.981
Anxious right now.

00:19:18.067 --> 00:19:20.042
Okay, anything else?

00:19:23.308 --> 00:19:25.063
Holy crap! What?!

00:19:29.595 --> 00:19:32.170
I just remembered, when I was a kid,

00:19:32.205 --> 00:19:34.951
I swallowed like eight things of pop
rocks, and then drank a whole can of coke.

00:19:35.036 --> 00:19:38.153
You don't think that that counts
as a suicide attempt, do you?

00:19:48.098 --> 00:19:49.513
You okay?

00:19:51.047 --> 00:19:52.250
Am I okay?

00:19:52.298 --> 00:19:53.183
Yeah.

00:19:53.237 --> 00:19:56.891
I just helped you steal some dead
guy's confidential psych files.

00:19:57.095 --> 00:19:58.612
I'm awesome!

00:20:00.065 --> 00:20:01.810
It started a little over a year ago.

00:20:02.298 --> 00:20:04.212
Migraines at first.

00:20:05.357 --> 00:20:08.392
Then I found I could do stuff.

00:20:08.467 --> 00:20:09.820
What do you mean, "do stuff"?

00:20:09.845 --> 00:20:11.230
I have this ability.

00:20:13.027 --> 00:20:14.622
When I touch something,

00:20:14.625 --> 00:20:16.850
I can electrocute it if I want.

00:20:37.828 --> 00:20:39.462
Oh, thank god you're okay.

00:20:46.525 --> 00:20:48.390
Oh, you're better than okay.

00:20:48.415 --> 00:20:50.930
Sam, you sly dog.

00:20:52.735 --> 00:20:54.880
What else does the yellow-Eyed man say?

00:20:55.406 --> 00:20:58.110
He has plans for me.

00:21:01.068 --> 00:21:02.973
He says there's a war coming,

00:21:03.515 --> 00:21:05.620
And people like me...

00:21:05.628 --> 00:21:07.560
We're gonna be the soldiers.

00:21:08.017 --> 00:21:10.281
Everything is about to change.

00:21:10.678 --> 00:21:13.563
He's not talking about us, right?

00:21:14.268 --> 00:21:15.991
Yeah, I think he is.

00:21:20.588 --> 00:21:23.870
Well... but how can we turn into that?

00:21:27.037 --> 00:21:28.042
I don't...

00:21:29.328 --> 00:21:30.600
Get down! Oh my god!

00:21:31.425 --> 00:21:32.953
Oh, my god, what's happening?

00:21:46.795 --> 00:21:47.650
Gordon!

00:21:54.705 --> 00:21:56.183
You do that to my brother,

00:21:56.186 --> 00:21:57.941
I'll kill you! Dean, wait!

00:22:17.075 --> 00:22:19.300
Wait, I don't understand.

00:22:19.408 --> 00:22:21.811
Shouldn't we be talking to the cops?

00:22:22.565 --> 00:22:24.872
Trust me, they wouldn't do us much good.

00:22:32.086 --> 00:22:34.901
These are 223 caliber, subsonic rounds.

00:22:34.987 --> 00:22:37.381
The guy must have put a
suppressor on the rifle.

00:22:39.028 --> 00:22:41.421
Dude, who are you?!

00:22:42.018 --> 00:22:44.290
Oh, I just, uh

00:22:44.807 --> 00:22:47.050
I just watch a lot of "T.J.Hooker".

00:22:52.065 --> 00:22:53.162
Who you calling?

00:22:53.197 --> 00:22:54.112
My brother.

00:22:54.205 --> 00:22:56.070
I think we definitely need help.

00:22:57.076 --> 00:22:58.060
Hello?

00:22:58.075 --> 00:23:00.150
Dean. Sam, I've been looking for you.

00:23:00.556 --> 00:23:02.743
Yeah, look, I'm in Indiana.

00:23:02.775 --> 00:23:04.902
Lafayette. I know.

00:23:05.005 --> 00:23:05.952
You do?

00:23:06.698 --> 00:23:08.230
Yeah, I talked to Ellen.

00:23:08.275 --> 00:23:10.033
I just got here myself.

00:23:10.367 --> 00:23:12.123
It's a real funky town.

00:23:12.545 --> 00:23:14.490
You ditched me, Sammy.

00:23:14.585 --> 00:23:17.880
Yeah, I'm sorry. Look, right now,

00:23:17.967 --> 00:23:19.813
There's someone after me. What? Who?

00:23:19.875 --> 00:23:21.952
I don't know. That's
what we need to find out.

00:23:22.678 --> 00:23:23.982
Where are you?

00:23:23.998 --> 00:23:27.892
I'm staying at 5637 Monroe
street. Why don't you meet me here?

00:23:27.947 --> 00:23:28.962
Yeah,  sure.

00:23:32.946 --> 00:23:34.373
Now, was that so hard?

00:23:35.037 --> 00:23:36.352
Bite me.

00:23:37.895 --> 00:23:39.031
What is it?

00:23:39.045 --> 00:23:40.451
My brother's in trouble.

00:23:40.605 --> 00:23:41.351
What?

00:23:42.017 --> 00:23:43.703
He gave me a code word.

00:23:44.107 --> 00:23:45.700
Someone's got a gun on him.

00:23:46.328 --> 00:23:48.322
Code word? Yeah.

00:23:48.347 --> 00:23:49.692
"Funky town"

00:23:51.395 --> 00:23:53.400
Well, he thought of it.

00:23:53.437 --> 00:23:54.373
It's kind of a

00:23:54.385 --> 00:23:55.560
Long story.

00:23:56.105 --> 00:23:57.070
Come on.

00:23:58.726 --> 00:23:59.663
Gordy,

00:23:59.668 --> 00:24:02.733
I know me and Sam ain't exactly
your favorite people, but,

00:24:03.076 --> 00:24:05.072
Don't you think this
is a little extreme?

00:24:05.568 --> 00:24:07.592
Oh, you think this is revenge?

00:24:08.415 --> 00:24:11.111
We did leave you tied up in
your own mess for three days.

00:24:11.216 --> 00:24:12.610
Which was awesome.

00:24:13.365 --> 00:24:15.350
Sorry, I shouldn't laugh. Yeah,

00:24:16.315 --> 00:24:18.973
I was definitely planning on
whupping your ass for that.

00:24:19.546 --> 00:24:22.301
That's not what this
is. This isn't personal.

00:24:23.566 --> 00:24:26.322
I'm not a killer, Dean.

00:24:26.765 --> 00:24:28.022
I'm a hunter.

00:24:29.006 --> 00:24:31.143
And your brother is fair game.

00:24:35.108 --> 00:24:36.600
I don't think I should leave.

00:24:36.658 --> 00:24:38.690
I want you out of harm's way, Ava.

00:24:39.185 --> 00:24:40.523
What about you?

00:24:40.617 --> 00:24:42.331
Harm's way doesn't really bother me.

00:24:42.346 --> 00:24:43.250
No, but,

00:24:43.258 --> 00:24:45.370
You are walking right into my vision.

00:24:45.386 --> 00:24:46.923
I mean, this is how you die!

00:24:46.955 --> 00:24:48.371
It doesn't matter.

00:24:49.915 --> 00:24:51.383
It's my brother.

00:24:51.716 --> 00:24:53.270
Maybe I can help.

00:24:53.326 --> 00:24:54.970
You've done all you can. Just...

00:24:55.498 --> 00:24:57.181
Just go back to your fianc.

00:24:58.477 --> 00:24:59.560
Are you sure?

00:25:00.587 --> 00:25:02.241
Yes, I'm sure.

00:25:02.535 --> 00:25:03.901
Go home, Ava.

00:25:03.968 --> 00:25:05.362
You'll be safe there.

00:25:10.015 --> 00:25:11.081
Well, just...

00:25:13.095 --> 00:25:14.643
Promise me you'll call, then.

00:25:14.655 --> 00:25:17.801
When you get your brother, just let
me know that everything's all right.

00:25:18.565 --> 00:25:19.833
I promise.

00:25:21.136 --> 00:25:24.250
See, I was doing an
exorcism down in Louisiana.

00:25:24.675 --> 00:25:27.391
A teenage girl. It seemed routine.

00:25:27.476 --> 00:25:29.112
Some low-Level demon.

00:25:29.175 --> 00:25:31.551
But between all the jabbering
and the head-Spinning,

00:25:31.596 --> 00:25:34.862
The damn thing muttered
something about a coming war.

00:25:34.897 --> 00:25:37.293
I don't think it meant to.
It just kind of slipped out.

00:25:37.327 --> 00:25:38.531
But it was too late.

00:25:38.577 --> 00:25:40.290
It piqued my interest.

00:25:40.338 --> 00:25:43.820
And you can really make a demon
talk when you got the right tools.

00:25:43.886 --> 00:25:46.143
What happened to the
girl it was possessing?

00:25:46.197 --> 00:25:47.653
She didn't make it.

00:25:49.217 --> 00:25:51.083
Well, you're a son of a bitch.

00:25:57.026 --> 00:25:59.051
That's my mama you're talking about.

00:26:00.598 --> 00:26:01.712
Anyway,

00:26:02.875 --> 00:26:06.911
This demon tells me they have
soldiers to fight in this coming war.

00:26:06.927 --> 00:26:09.560
Humans fighting on hell's
side. You believe that?

00:26:09.966 --> 00:26:13.972
I mean, they're psychics, so they're
not exactly pure humans. But still,

00:26:14.005 --> 00:26:18.000
What kind of worthless scumbag you got
to be to turn against your own race?

00:26:19.975 --> 00:26:21.911
But you know the
biggest kick in the ass?

00:26:22.428 --> 00:26:24.663
This demon said I knew one of them

00:26:25.507 --> 00:26:28.203
Our very own Sammy Winchester.

00:26:31.547 --> 00:26:32.583
Well, this is...

00:26:32.665 --> 00:26:34.753
This is a whole new level of moronic,

00:26:34.846 --> 00:26:36.602
Even for you. Yeah?

00:26:37.728 --> 00:26:39.070
Come on, Dean.

00:26:39.075 --> 00:26:40.423
I know

00:26:40.427 --> 00:26:42.493
About Sam's visions.

00:26:43.987 --> 00:26:45.991
I know everything. Really?

00:26:46.386 --> 00:26:48.260
Because a demon told you?

00:26:48.425 --> 00:26:50.831
Yeah, and it wasn't lying. Hey, Dean,

00:26:51.305 --> 00:26:54.583
I'm not some reckless yahoo,
okay? I did my homework.

00:26:54.685 --> 00:26:56.411
I made damn sure it was true.

00:26:57.076 --> 00:26:59.941
Look, you got your
Roadhouse connections.

00:27:00.375 --> 00:27:01.661
I got mine.

00:27:02.068 --> 00:27:04.612
It's how I found Sammy
in the first place.

00:27:12.528 --> 00:27:16.050
About a month ago, I found another
one of these freaks here in town.

00:27:16.088 --> 00:27:18.642
He could deep-Fry a person
just by touching them.

00:27:18.675 --> 00:27:20.111
Yeah, did he kill anyone?

00:27:20.205 --> 00:27:22.790
Besides mr. Tinkles, the cat, no.

00:27:22.856 --> 00:27:24.563
But he was working up to it.

00:27:25.525 --> 00:27:27.361
They're all gonna be killers, Dean.

00:27:27.387 --> 00:27:28.922
We got to take them all out,

00:27:28.928 --> 00:27:31.050
And that means Sammy too.

00:27:36.005 --> 00:27:38.321
You think Sam's stupid enough
to walk through that front door?

00:27:38.395 --> 00:27:40.102
No, I don't.

00:27:40.476 --> 00:27:43.170
Especially since I'm sure
you found a way to warn him.

00:27:45.568 --> 00:27:47.721
You really think I'm that stupid?

00:27:53.597 --> 00:27:54.732
No,

00:27:55.627 --> 00:27:58.153
Sammy's gonna scope the place first,

00:27:59.007 --> 00:28:01.161
See me covering the front door.

00:28:02.558 --> 00:28:04.602
So he's gonna take the back.

00:28:05.596 --> 00:28:08.020
And when he does,
he'll hit the tripwire.

00:28:09.606 --> 00:28:10.822
Then...

00:28:15.727 --> 00:28:16.952
Boom.

00:28:18.156 --> 00:28:20.851
Sam's not gonna fall
for a frickin' tripwire.

00:28:22.038 --> 00:28:23.431
Maybe you're right.

00:28:26.538 --> 00:28:28.462
That's why I'll have a second one.

00:28:34.297 --> 00:28:35.481
Hey, look,

00:28:36.526 --> 00:28:37.862
I'm sorry.

00:28:38.637 --> 00:28:41.192
I wish I didn't have
to do this. I really do.

00:28:42.316 --> 00:28:43.942
But for what it's worth,

00:28:45.065 --> 00:28:46.703
It will be quick.

00:29:19.027 --> 00:29:20.173
Come on, man.

00:29:20.897 --> 00:29:23.433
I know Sam, okay? Better than anyone.

00:29:23.906 --> 00:29:25.830
He's got more of a
conscience than I do. I mean,

00:29:25.868 --> 00:29:27.830
The guy feels guilty surfing
the internet for porn.

00:29:27.865 --> 00:29:28.851
Maybe you're right,

00:29:29.517 --> 00:29:31.522
But one day, he's gonna be a monster.

00:29:31.556 --> 00:29:32.322
How?

00:29:32.826 --> 00:29:35.071
Huh? How's a guy like
Sam become a monster?

00:29:35.096 --> 00:29:37.820
It beats me, but he will.
No, you don't know that!

00:29:39.457 --> 00:29:41.040
I'm surprised at you, Dean.

00:29:41.628 --> 00:29:43.200
Getting all emotional.

00:29:44.216 --> 00:29:47.142
I had heard you were more
of a professional than this.

00:29:50.058 --> 00:29:50.982
Look,

00:29:50.995 --> 00:29:55.071
Let's say you're cruising
around in that car of yours.

00:29:55.105 --> 00:29:56.301
And uh,

00:29:56.507 --> 00:30:00.031
You have little Hitler
riding shotgun, right?

00:30:00.556 --> 00:30:02.000
Back when he was just some

00:30:02.006 --> 00:30:04.460
Goofy, crappy artist.

00:30:05.048 --> 00:30:08.452
But you knew what he was
gonna turn into someday.

00:30:09.358 --> 00:30:10.853
You'd take him out.

00:30:11.235 --> 00:30:13.033
No questions, am I right?

00:30:13.077 --> 00:30:14.823
That's not Sam. Yes, it is.

00:30:15.606 --> 00:30:17.401
You just can't see it yet.

00:30:20.008 --> 00:30:22.562
Dean, it's his destiny.

00:30:25.585 --> 00:30:26.661
Look,

00:30:26.665 --> 00:30:28.583
I'm sympathetic.

00:30:29.038 --> 00:30:30.890
He's your brother. You love the guy.

00:30:31.575 --> 00:30:34.021
This has got to hurt like hell for you.

00:30:39.566 --> 00:30:41.252
But here's the thing.

00:30:43.828 --> 00:30:45.332
It would have wrecked him,

00:30:46.447 --> 00:30:47.653
But your dad

00:30:49.078 --> 00:30:50.861
If it really came right down to it,

00:30:50.905 --> 00:30:53.561
He would have had the stones
to do the right thing here.

00:30:54.596 --> 00:30:56.200
So, you're telling me

00:30:57.056 --> 00:30:59.010
You're not the man he is?

00:32:16.716 --> 00:32:18.061
You hear him?

00:32:31.768 --> 00:32:33.233
Here he comes.

00:32:39.715 --> 00:32:40.863
Hold on.

00:32:41.277 --> 00:32:42.713
Not yet.

00:32:43.517 --> 00:32:45.201
Let's wait and see.

00:33:08.655 --> 00:33:09.982
Sorry, Dean.

00:33:34.588 --> 00:33:35.983
Drop the gun.

00:33:37.287 --> 00:33:39.550
You shouldn't take your
shoes off around here.

00:33:39.898 --> 00:33:42.462
You might get tetanus. Put it down now!

00:33:49.907 --> 00:33:51.521
You wouldn't shoot me, would you, Sammy?

00:33:52.295 --> 00:33:55.211
'Cause your brother, he thinks
you're some kind of saint.

00:33:55.616 --> 00:33:56.812
Yeah.

00:33:56.906 --> 00:33:58.110
Well, I wouldn't be so sure.

00:33:59.036 --> 00:34:00.800
See, that's what I said.

00:34:25.247 --> 00:34:28.170
You're no better than the
filthy things you hunt.

00:34:46.077 --> 00:34:47.182
Do it.

00:34:48.008 --> 00:34:49.222
Do it!

00:34:49.707 --> 00:34:52.292
Show your brother the
killer you really are, Sammy.

00:35:00.648 --> 00:35:02.122
It's Sam.

00:35:34.056 --> 00:35:36.972
Son of a bitch... Dean, no.

00:35:37.416 --> 00:35:39.872
I let him live once. I'm not
making the same mistake twice.

00:35:39.968 --> 00:35:40.960
Trust me.

00:35:41.588 --> 00:35:43.402
Gordon's taken care of.

00:35:45.016 --> 00:35:46.030
Come on.

00:36:08.806 --> 00:36:10.432
You call this taken care of?

00:36:15.087 --> 00:36:16.293
What the hell are we doing?

00:36:16.355 --> 00:36:17.973
Just trust me on this. All right?

00:36:25.867 --> 00:36:28.201
Drop your weapons!
Get down on your knees!

00:36:28.237 --> 00:36:29.573
Do it now!

00:36:40.056 --> 00:36:41.592
Put your hands on your head.

00:36:42.668 --> 00:36:44.160
Easy now.

00:37:03.036 --> 00:37:04.741
Anonymous tip.

00:37:05.505 --> 00:37:08.123
You're a fine, upstanding citizen, Sam.

00:37:20.588 --> 00:37:22.232
Gordon Walker was hunting Sam?

00:37:22.246 --> 00:37:23.603
And he almost killed us both 'cause

00:37:23.635 --> 00:37:25.613
Somebody over there can't
keep their frickin' mouth shut.

00:37:26.018 --> 00:37:27.962
And you honestly think that it was me?

00:37:28.458 --> 00:37:29.352
Or Ash or Jo?

00:37:29.356 --> 00:37:30.242
No way.

00:37:30.278 --> 00:37:31.802
Who else knows about Sam, huh?

00:37:33.005 --> 00:37:34.822
Well, you must have
been talking to somebody.

00:37:34.875 --> 00:37:36.961
You can say a lot of things about us

00:37:37.038 --> 00:37:38.292
But we aren't disloyal,

00:37:38.297 --> 00:37:39.651
And we're not stupid.

00:37:39.687 --> 00:37:41.363
We haven't breathed a word of this.

00:37:41.427 --> 00:37:43.443
Gordon said he had
Roadhouse connections, Ellen.

00:37:43.456 --> 00:37:46.243
And this Roadhouse is
full of other hunters.

00:37:47.816 --> 00:37:50.670
They're all smart.
They're good trackers,

00:37:50.716 --> 00:37:53.631
Each of them with their own
patterns and connections.

00:37:53.687 --> 00:37:56.011
Hell, I could name 12 of them right now

00:37:56.018 --> 00:37:58.102
That are capable of
putting this together.

00:38:00.336 --> 00:38:02.673
I am sorry about what happened, Dean,

00:38:03.535 --> 00:38:05.521
But I can't control these people

00:38:05.527 --> 00:38:07.682
Or what they choose to believe.

00:38:13.995 --> 00:38:16.163
Hey, Ava, it's Sam... again.

00:38:17.047 --> 00:38:18.180
Call me when you get this.

00:38:18.286 --> 00:38:20.452
Just want to make
sure you got home okay.

00:38:20.985 --> 00:38:22.543
All right, bye.

00:38:22.557 --> 00:38:24.170
Everything all right?

00:38:24.955 --> 00:38:27.043
Yeah, I hope so.

00:38:27.076 --> 00:38:30.212
Well, Gordon should be reaching for the
soap for the next few years, at least.

00:38:30.297 --> 00:38:31.203
Yeah,

00:38:31.567 --> 00:38:34.071
If they pin Scott
Carey's murder on him...

00:38:34.558 --> 00:38:36.293
And if he doesn't bust out.

00:38:38.885 --> 00:38:41.200
Dude, you ever take
off like that again...

00:38:43.078 --> 00:38:44.210
What?

00:38:44.396 --> 00:38:45.850
You'd kill me?

00:38:47.005 --> 00:38:48.643
That's so not funny.

00:38:49.687 --> 00:38:50.660
All right.

00:38:51.367 --> 00:38:53.633
All right. So, where to next then?

00:38:53.665 --> 00:38:54.701
One word,

00:38:55.187 --> 00:38:57.120
Amsterdam. Dean...

00:38:57.166 --> 00:38:59.812
Come on, man, I hear the coffee
shops don't even serve coffee.

00:38:59.916 --> 00:39:02.252
I'm not gonna just ditch
the job. Screw the job.

00:39:02.798 --> 00:39:04.940
Screw it, man. I'm
sick of the job anyway.

00:39:04.997 --> 00:39:06.053
We don't get paid.

00:39:06.087 --> 00:39:07.191
We don't get thanked.

00:39:07.277 --> 00:39:08.762
The only thing we get is bad luck.

00:39:09.446 --> 00:39:11.210
Well, come on dude, you're a hunter.

00:39:11.316 --> 00:39:13.582
I mean, it's what you were meant to
do. I wasn't meant to do anything.

00:39:13.618 --> 00:39:15.390
I don't believe in that destiny crap.

00:39:15.468 --> 00:39:17.541
You mean you don't
believe in my destiny.

00:39:18.818 --> 00:39:19.990
Whatever.

00:39:21.165 --> 00:39:22.981
Look, Dean, I've tried running before.

00:39:23.415 --> 00:39:25.981
I mean, I ran all the way to
California, and look what happened.

00:39:26.748 --> 00:39:28.311
You can't run from this,

00:39:28.318 --> 00:39:29.992
And you can't protect me.

00:39:32.528 --> 00:39:33.852
I can try.

00:39:36.525 --> 00:39:37.930
Thanks for that.

00:39:42.377 --> 00:39:44.453
Look, Dean, I'm gonna keep hunting.

00:39:45.376 --> 00:39:46.662
I mean, whatever's coming,

00:39:47.286 --> 00:39:50.410
I'm taking it head on so if
you really want to watch my back

00:39:51.048 --> 00:39:52.820
Then I guess you're gonna
have to stick around.

00:39:53.546 --> 00:39:55.392
Bitch. Jerk.

00:40:02.036 --> 00:40:03.500
You calling that Ava girl again?

00:40:03.528 --> 00:40:05.110
You sweet on her or something?

00:40:06.457 --> 00:40:08.171
She's engaged, Dean.

00:40:08.216 --> 00:40:09.252
So?

00:40:09.837 --> 00:40:11.050
What's the point in saving the world,

00:40:11.056 --> 00:40:13.132
If you can't get a little
nookie once in a while, huh?

00:40:16.136 --> 00:40:17.373
What?

00:40:18.375 --> 00:40:19.753
Just a feeling.

00:40:22.015 --> 00:40:24.231
How far is it to Peoria?

00:40:34.098 --> 00:40:34.972
Hello?

00:40:38.086 --> 00:40:39.650
Is anybody home?

00:40:51.585 --> 00:40:52.892
My god...

00:41:09.755 --> 00:41:10.783
Hey.

00:41:14.195 --> 00:41:15.622
Sulfur.

00:41:19.187 --> 00:41:20.691
The demon's been here.

00:41:42.077 --> 00:41:43.472
Ava...



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
